00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:23,280
只要我看见头 我就知道那只鸟大不大
I know a small tip when I see one.

342
00:16:25,660 --> 00:16:26,180
看这里
Here.

343
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:30,860
抱歉 抱歉
Sorry, sorry.

344
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:33,660
她刚给我看了安妮·海瑟薇的新发型
She just showed me a picture of Anne Hathaway's new haircut.

345
00:16:37,460 --> 00:16:38,800
这不错
Well, this is good,

346
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:40,420
因为能证明那女人在撒谎
because it can proves that woman is lying.

347
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:42,520
对啊 你可以把这拿给皮尔斯看
Yep, you just have to show this to Piers.

348
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:45,860
我说过 我绝不会提及[靠近]我爸的鸡鸡
I told you, I'm not going near my father's penis.

349
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:49,100
我只需指出
All I have to do is point out

350
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:51,080
那女人根本不懂理财和金融
that that woman has no finance skills.

351
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:52,880
不像她 我们要采取高尚的手段
Unlike her, we are taking the high road.

352
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:55,220
麦克斯 你是把照片发你手机上吗
Max, are you sending that to yourself?

353
00:16:59,700 --> 00:17:01,240
今天的嘉宾是珊卓拉·罗森索
I'm here with Sandra Rosenthal,

354
00:17:01,540 --> 00:17:02,920
她刚签了一份超值钱的书约
Who's just signed a huge book deal

355
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:04,100
揭发臭名昭著的金融家
to do a kiss-and-tell

356
00:17:04,100 --> 00:17:06,280
马丁·钱宁的种种隐私
on disgraced financier Martin Channing.

357
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:08,300
-欢迎你 珊卓拉 -你好 皮尔斯
- Welcome to you, Sandra. - Hello, piers.

358
00:17:08,600 --> 00:17:10,660
谢谢你邀请我上台讲述我的故事
Thank you for allowing me to tell my story.

359
00:17:10,660 --> 00:17:12,500
只是个故事而已
It's a story, all right.

360
00:17:13,020 --> 00:17:14,280
我们十分想听
Wow, so we're right into it.

361
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:15,120
好的 让我先介绍下
Okay, well, let me catch up.

362
00:17:15,140 --> 00:17:16,860
另一位嘉宾是卡洛琳·钱宁
My other guest is Caroline Channing,

363
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,560
马丁·钱宁的女儿 说得委婉些
daughter of martin Channing, who, to put it mildly,

364
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:21,680
她声称罗森索女士的书
is claiming that your book, Ms. Rosenthal,

365
00:17:21,740 --> 00:17:23,440
完全就是狗屁连篇
is a bunch of bull.

366
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:24,560
没错 皮尔斯
That's right, Piers.

367
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:25,860
按你们英国人的说法
It's pure rubbish,

368
00:17:25,860 --> 00:17:27,200
就是"通篇胡扯"
as your people say.

369
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:30,300
那完全是你们美国人的说法
That was perfectly American.

370
00:17:32,020 --> 00:17:33,500
好吧 那先从你开始
Right, then, let me start with you.

371
00:17:33,940 --> 00:17:36,400
事情是这样的 推动罗森索女士作品的
Well, to catch everybody up, Ms. Rosenthal's large book advance

372
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:38,740
最"大"动力 是她揭露某物的真相是...
really has to do with something that turned out to be,

373
00:17:38,740 --> 00:17:40,600
用你的话来说 "非常小"
by your words, very small.

374
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:41,621
有何评论 钱宁小姐
Comments, Ms. Channing?

375
00:17:45,460 --> 00:17:47,440
我不发表任何评论 皮尔斯
I'd rather not comment about that, Piers,

376
00:17:47,520 --> 00:17:49,840
因为我有格调 但我的确有个问题
because I have class, but I do have a question

377
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:52,100
要问我父亲曾经聘用过的珊卓拉女士
for Ms. Rosenthal, who was hired by my father

378
00:17:52,100 --> 00:17:54,420
因为她声称自己是金融学的学士
because she claimed she had a degree in finance.

379
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:57,980
珊卓拉女士 一辆载有27个人的火车
Ms. Rosenthal, if a train carrying 27 passengers

380
00:17:57,980 --> 00:18:00,440
早上9点离开中央车站
leaves Grand Central Station at 9:00 A.M.,

381
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:04,180
于下午5点到达800英里外的芝加哥
travels 800 miles to Chicago, arriving at 5:00 p.M.,

382
00:18:04,180 --> 00:18:05,640
请问火车的速度是多少
how fast was it traveling?

383
00:18:05,671 --> 00:18:07,830
这个嘛
Well, I--

384
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:08,820
超简单的数学题 皮尔斯
Simple math, piers.

385
00:18:09,340 --> 00:18:10,300
每小时100英里
100 miles an hour.

386
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:12,660
-你说什么 -你问题的答案
- I'm sorry? - That's your answer.

387
00:18:12,740 --> 00:18:14,220
抱歉 我也算是个数学高手
Sorry, I'm a bit of a mathlete.

388
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:16,360
真厉害
Impressive.

389
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:18,640
我也有个数学问题要问你
I've got a math equation for you.

390
00:18:19,040 --> 00:18:21,480
如果一辆3英寸长的"火车"开进"隧道"
If a 3-inch train is entering a tunnel,

391
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:22,720
那"隧道"能感觉到吗
do I even know it's there?

392
00:18:24,220 --> 00:18:26,100
女士们 这不是毛里·波维奇无下限的节目
Ladies, this isn't Maury Povich.

393
00:18:28,840 --> 00:18:30,620
皮尔斯 我只是单纯想说明
Piers, I am simply trying to illustrate

394
00:18:30,620 --> 00:18:32,280
如果她够格胜任金融工作的话
that she should have been able to answer it,

395
00:18:32,520 --> 00:18:34,200
她应该可以回答那个问题才对
had she been qualified for her job in finance.

396
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:39,160
我书里所写的一切内容都是真的
Everything that I am writing in the book is true, Piers.

397
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:41,200
我说的任何东西
There is nothing that I have said

398
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:42,840
她都无法证明是假的
that she can prove is untrue.

399
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:49,840
等下 为什么会有个女人在我桌子底下
Wait a minute, why is there a woman under my desk?

400
00:18:51,040 --> 00:18:52,140
有吗 皮尔斯
Oh, is there, Piers?

401
00:18:53,380 --> 00:18:55,840
没错 我的父亲是骗了很多人的钱
Yes, my father defrauded a lot of people,

402
00:18:55,840 --> 00:18:57,160
他也为此付出了代价
and he's paying a price for that,

403
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:59,600
但她为了自己的利益而消费我父亲时
but I'm not gonna sit by silently while she exploits him

404
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:01,240
我绝对不会袖手旁观
With lies for her own gain.

405
00:19:01,740 --> 00:19:03,340
皮尔斯 我想告诉您
Piers, there's so much about my father

406
00:19:03,340 --> 00:19:05,980
很多关于我父亲的事情 比如...
I want you to know, like he--

407
00:19:11,240 --> 00:19:12,400
这是什么
What is this?

408
00:19:12,620 --> 00:19:14,780
我知道这是什么
Well...I know what this is.

409
00:19:14,940 --> 00:19:15,700
我也有一根
I've got one.

410
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:18,900
但这是谁的 为什么要给我看
But whose is it, and why am I looking at it?

411
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:20,540
那是我父亲的
It's my father's.

412
00:19:21,320 --> 00:19:22,940
他的"鸟"不小心探头了
He had a bit of a tip slip.

413
00:19:24,660 --> 00:19:26,580
女士 我不知道你想要什么样的男人
Madam, I don't know what you're looking for in a man,

414
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:29,040
但这个男人
but this...

415
00:19:29,900 --> 00:19:31,640
明显是"神雕大侠"
is far from inadequate.

416
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:36,260
老实说 与你描述差距太远
In fact, it's so far from inadequate,

417
00:19:36,260 --> 00:19:38,960
我要马上结束本期访谈
that I'm bringing this interview to an immediate close.

418
00:19:39,060 --> 00:19:42,040
你和你的书都没有任何可信度
Your book and you lack any credibility.

419
00:19:42,860 --> 00:19:44,140
到此为止
That's it.

420
00:19:48,280 --> 00:19:50,580
"你能帮我搞到皮尔斯家具店的折扣吗"
"Can you hook me up with a discount at Piers 1 Imports?"

421
00:19:56,980 --> 00:19:58,720
很可能某天出版商会对你有兴趣
Hey, you know, they'll probably come to you one day

422
00:19:58,740 --> 00:19:59,841
想出一本你的揭秘书
and want a tell-all book.

423
00:20:00,020 --> 00:20:02,560
记住第一章已经有了 "边睡觉边放屁"
Remember, we already have chapter one, "Sleep farts."

424
00:20:03,900 --> 00:20:06,140
第二章是 "我的新后妈 麦克斯"
Chapter two: "My new stepmom Max."

425
00:20:09,660 --> 00:20:11,820
麦克斯 我会一辈子都得替我爸辩护吗
Max, am I gonna have to defend my father forever?

426
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:13,860
可能吧 但别担心
Probably, but don't worry,

427
00:20:13,860 --> 00:20:15,980
-我会帮你的 -谢谢
- I'll be there to help. - Thank you.

428
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:18,200
因为保卫丈夫 是妻子的职责
'cause it's a wife's job to defend her husband.

429
00:20:20,580 --> 00:20:22,700
我一想到他要在监狱度过余生
It makes me sad to think he's gonna be in prison

430
00:20:22,700 --> 00:20:23,840
就觉得很难过
for the rest of his life.

431
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:26,900
别这样想嘛 他不是在监狱
Don't think of it like that. He's not just in prison.

432
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:29,280
他是在非洲跟联合国儿童基金会共事
He's in Africa working with UNICEF,

433
00:20:29,560 --> 00:20:30,440
他在海地
He's in Haiti,

434
00:20:30,740 --> 00:20:32,600
他在"富人湖"上滑水
he's water-skiing on "Lake rich person,"

435
00:20:32,980 --> 00:20:35,100
他还在我电脑的桌面上
and he's on the desktop of my computer.

436
00:20:37,520 --> 00:20:38,920
我应该删掉那照片
I should delete that.

437
00:20:40,260 --> 00:20:41,000
我的手机放哪里了
Where'd I leave my phone?

438
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:47,120
天啊 你们不会是在看我爸的照片吧
Oh, god, are you guys looking at the picture of my dad?

439
00:20:47,420 --> 00:20:49,120
是的 钦佩不已啊
We are. Respect.

440
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:53,020
敬仰之情有如滔滔江水 连绵不绝
So very much respect.

441
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:56,520
我见过更棒的
Eh, I've seen better.

442
00:20:57,840 --> 00:20:58,660
每天低头就能看见
Every day.

443
00:21:01,820 --> 00:21:03,620
还给人家啦
Give me that.
